<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.claude.deploy-live — the AUTONOMOUS deploy lane (LAND_PIPELINE_V2 §4.3). Every 600s:
  advance the live checkout to the newest origin/main commit whose TREE carries a GREEN post-land
  stamp, run install.sh, then run the host-suite partition against the now-live layer. Nothing is
  stamped green ⇒ silent exit 0; no verification net ⇒ ONE damped page per 24h. This is the first
  time the live layer only ever advances to a full-suite-proven tree (R3) — the manual `git pull
  --ff-only` it replaces deployed whatever happened to be on origin/main.

  `bash -c` (not a bare ProgramArguments path) for the same two reasons as postland-verify: launchd
  expands neither ~ nor $HOME inside ProgramArguments, and its PATH has no Homebrew — where git,
  bats and timeout(1) actually live. Standard*Path CANNOT take $HOME at all, hence the literal.

  THE EXEC TARGET FALLS BACK TO THE REPO COPY, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING (I11 — existence-check the
  platter; the same fix hooks/operator-readout.sh:238-246 carries). ~/.claude/scripts/deploy-live.sh
  is a SYMLINK that deploy-live.sh itself creates, via link_refresh → install.sh, so the advancer was
  undeployable by its own outage: with the link absent the job could not start AT ALL. Measured on
  this host: 59 × `cannot execute: No such file or directory`, and the link only appeared at 10:32 on
  2026-07-29, four minutes after the newest failure line — i.e. by luck, not by design. The repo path
  is what the symlink points AT, so this is correct in both states and prefers the live layer when it
  exists. It is $HOME-relative and matches deploy-live.sh's own DEPLOY_REPO default.

  RunAtLoad true: a login/boot is exactly when the live layer is most likely to be stale, and one
  tick is cheap (an already-deployed tick is a fetch + a rev-parse). C10: OPERATOR loads it, via
  docs/activation/pending-activation/14-land-pipeline-v2-activate.sh.
  Kill switch: launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.claude.deploy-live
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.claude.deploy-live</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>export PATH="$HOME/.claude/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"; D="$HOME/.claude/scripts/deploy-live.sh"; [ -x "$D" ] || D="$HOME/Development/claude-infrastructure/scripts/deploy-live.sh"; exec "$D" --auto</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>600</integer>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>LowPriorityIO</key>
    <true/>

    <key>Nice</key>
    <integer>10</integer>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/autonomy/postland/deploy.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/autonomy/postland/deploy.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
